      "writtenOn": "2019-04-25T18:24:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is the default voltage when PD isn\u0027t enabled or available.\n\nFrom the Type-C spec, Release 1.4:\nThree current level advertisements at 5V VBUS are defined by USB Type-C Current:\n  1) Default is the as-configured for high-power operation current value as defined by a\nUSB Specification (500 mA for USB 2.0 ports; 900 mA or 1,500 mA for USB 3.2 ports\noperating in single-lane or dual-lane, respectively)\n  2) USB Type-C Current @ 1.5 A\n  3) USB Type-C Current @ 3.0 A\n\nSee Table 2-1 in the Type-C spec, Release 1.4 for more details.",
      "parentUuid": "6b2ba200_749d04ce",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 56,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 59,
